Intermittent, timing-dependent failure only observed under the full concurrent test suite (not reproducible in isolation): z3-4.14.1 emits an undocumented diagnostic comment line (e.g. "; :expand-definitions line: 1 position: 1") on stdout immediately after each "unsupported" response to an unrecognized option, which jSMTLIB's response parser normally strips as a standard SMT-LIB ';' comment; under concurrent solver-process load a fragment of that comment line (e.g. the word "position") occasionally leaks into the parsed response for the next command instead of being fully consumed with the first, producing a spurious mismatch against the golden -- a solver-process stream-reading race, not a defect in the test or golden Confirmed by reading SolverProcess.StreamGobbler.run(): its read loop offers a chunk to the queue as soon as endsWith() sees a balanced/terminated buffer, decoupled from whether a consumer is currently waiting -- a stray comment line with no unbalanced parens satisfies that immediately on its own if it happens to arrive as a separate OS-level read after the real response was already finalized, so it gets queued as a standalone chunk that the NEXT listen() call then consumes first. A real fix would need stdout to debounce/settle similarly to how errorSettleMillis already does for stderr, at a latency cost paid on every command for every solver, not just the rare versions that emit this quirk -- not attempted without sign-off given that tradeoff.

See https://github.com/smtlib/jSMTLIB/issues/99.
